Below is the framework I use for a professional Klaviyo audit (this is the same structure top-tier agencies and consultants use). You can send me the data, screenshots, exports, or grant descriptions and I’ll run the full audit using this framework.

Klaviyo Audit Framework (Complete, Agency-Grade)

1. Account Health & Infrastructure

Goal: Ensure the client’s foundation is solid before looking at flows or campaigns.
I will review:

✔ Deliverability & Sending Reputation

* Sending domain warm status
* SPF, DKIM, DMARC alignment
* Dedicated vs shared domain
* Google Postmaster Tools reputation
* Microsoft SNDS, blocklists, spam traps
* Bounce rates, unsubscribe rates, complaint rates
* Average inbox placement indicators

✔ List Hygiene

* Total profiles vs active profiles
* Suppressed count (and whether they should be deleted to reduce billed MAUs)
* Percent of profiles with email vs SMS
* Engaged segment definitions
* Sunset policy
* Compliance with Gmail 2024/2025 rules

✔ Integration Health

* Shopify/Recharge/Attentive/Custom API sync
* Product/catalog sync
* Metrics properly flowing (Started Checkout, Viewed Product, Placed Order, Subscription events, etc.)

⸻

2. Segmentation & Data Structure

Goal: Ensure the brand can personalize messaging rather than blast generic campaigns.

✔ Profile Properties

* Are forms collecting the right data?
* Are useful preferences being stored?
* Are there product-matching identifiers?
* Are subscriptions tracked as properties?

✔ Segmentation Structure

* Recency–Frequency–Monetary (RFM) segments
* New vs returning buyers
* VIP & loyalty segments
* Subscription lifecycle segments
* Cross-sell segments
* Lapsed and win-back segments

✔ Recommended Segments

I’ll create all suggested segments with exact Klaviyo definitions so you can implement instantly.

⸻

3. Flow Audit (Revenue & Strategy)

I review each flow for:

* Performance (open, click, placed order, revenue per recipient)
* Logic errors
* Trigger conditions
* Filters that restrict sends
* Missing essential flows
* Timing & message cadence
* A/B testing setup
* Creative, copy, and offer strategy
* Personalization opportunities

Core Flows I Review

* Welcome Series
* Browse Abandonment
* Cart Abandonment
* Checkout Abandonment
* Post-Purchase (1st time + repeat)
* Subscription lifecycle (Recharge/Stay/Skio)
* Win-back / Lapsed Buyer
* Product Review/Upsell
* Back-in-stock / Price drop
* Post-delivery review/education
* VIP flows

Flow Benchmark Comparison

I’ll compare each flow’s performance to:

* Klaviyo benchmarks
* Industry averages
* High-performing DTC benchmarks

⸻

4. Campaign Audit

Goal: Evaluate how campaigns actually perform over time.

I’ll analyze the last 90–180 days:

* Send frequency
* Engagement trends
* Revenue per campaign
* Deliverability decay
* Seasonal patterns
* Segment usage
* Click-to-open ratio
* Conversion rate
* Revenue per recipient

I’ll catch patterns like:

* Sending too often
* Not sending enough
* Sending to unengaged profiles
* No segmentation (blast campaigns)
* Heavy reliance on discounts
* Weak subject lines
* No pre-headers
* Off-brand design
* Overlapping segments causing double sends

⸻

5. Revenue Share by Channel

I’ll calculate:

* % of total revenue from email
* % from flows vs campaigns
* % from SMS
* Industry benchmarks
* Expected revenue gap

Goal: Quantify how much money they should be making — and identify the missing revenue.

⸻

6. Conversion & Retention Diagnostics

Especially important for subscription brands or brands with repeat purchase expectations.

I evaluate:

* Repeat purchase rate
* Time to 2nd order
* AOV trends
* CLTV segments
* Cohort performance
* Subscription churn + reasons
* Upsell/cross-sell opportunities
* Win-back performance

⸻

7. Compliance & Technical Setup

* Domain setup
* Link tracking parameters
* SMS opt-in compliance
* Signup forms
* Cookie consent rules
* Data consent

